// Scoped to the App target's Release configuration only (see baseConfigurationReference in
// App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj) -- mirrors Let Them Eat Cake's proven ios/release.xcconfig
// pattern exactly. Deliberately NOT passed as xcodebuild command-line overrides in
// .github/workflows/ios-release.yml: those apply to every target in the build graph (including
// auto-generated SPM resource-bundle targets that can't be signed at all), and headless
// `xcodebuild archive` resolves Automatic signing to "development" purpose for every target
// regardless of the archive action, causing signing-identity conflicts. Scoping via xcconfig
// avoids both problems.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is the shared Let Them Eat family Apple Developer Team ID (not a secret --
// reused as-is from Cake/Ramen's own release.xcconfig). PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER names a
// profile that must still be created in the Apple Developer portal for com.letthemeatcookies.app
// specifically -- profiles are bound 1:1 to a bundle ID and cannot be reused across apps, unlike
// the Distribution certificate and Team ID above it.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Distribution
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = J48FJJ3ABL
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER = Let Them Eat Cookies App Store
